@startuml
title Backfill Using Daily Parking Records
start
:Scheduled worker captures today's Sydney date;
:Build inclusive rolling date window backwards;
:Find eligible facility/date records within request budget;
while (eligible work remains?) is (yes)
  :Atomically claim ParkingDay with lease;
  :Fetch upstream history for facility and Sydney date;
  if (request successful?) then (yes)
    :Convert upstream timestamps to UTC Instants;
    :Upsert newest sample in each Sydney 10-minute bucket;
    :Set same ParkingDay state to COMPLETE;
    note right: Empty result is also COMPLETE.
  else (no)
    :Set same ParkingDay state to RETRY_WAIT;
    :Record retryAfter;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:Return;
stop

note right
  The compound key is (facilityId, sydneyDate). Missing document/state
  means not fetched. PROCESSING is protected by leaseUntil; expired
  leases can be reclaimed. COMPLETE dates are skipped; due retries
  are eligible again.

  The daily record contains both the bounded samples and durable
  backfill status. There is no separate marker collection or cursor.
  If a worker fails after sample upsert, repeating the request is safe.

  The worker scans today down through the configured inclusive window,
  caps requests per run, and rotates facility tie-breaking for fairness.
end note
@enduml
